Preserve symmetric length-prefixed metric h=-eta, trace, normal_order, sandwich_srednicki domains and signatures. Add try_trace_with<A:Coefficient>, try_trace and try_trace_exact via one generic pairing recurrence. Trace hard algorithm cap 12 even with larger user limits. Validate label bytes/word length before odd or empty shortcuts. Add typed bounded generic normal ordering and Srednicki sandwich where practical, sandwich hard cap 8. Existing functions expect checked paths. Preserve independent matrix oracle tests and legacy corpus. No gamma5/dummy summation/new eta convention.
Legacy expect wrappers use polynomial legacy_budget, avoiding a new global 1M operation limit; try_* uses caller budget. Hard word caps remain.
Reject known resource failures before owned key allocation. Reserve constructor/insertion logical work before cloning or formatting keys. Metric encoding must use a shared preflighted variable builder with no second constructor charge. Negation computes checked coefficient negation before cloning its key. Budgets are finite deterministic logical charges, not allocator/heap/CPU guarantees. Test large-key failure paths with thread-local allocation-size observation.
